# ASCII hyphen only

In frontend UI copy, metadata (titles, descriptions, OG, JSON-LD), articles, authors, and site config strings visible to users or crawlers, the **only** allowed dash character is U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS `-`.

## Replace with `-`

Never use em/en dashes, figure dash, horizontal bar, Unicode hyphen, non-breaking hyphen, minus sign, fullwidth/small hyphen variants, Hebrew maqaf, or any other `Pd` / dash lookalike.

| BAD | GOOD |
|-----|------|
| `F12 — חדשות` | `F12 - חדשות` |
| `3–6 חודשים` | `3-6 חודשים` |
| `פרופ־טק` | `פרופ-טק` |
| `title: "אירו—דולר"` | `title: "אירו-דולר"` |

## Scope

- Apply in `src/`, content, SEO helpers, and public text metadata.
- Do not introduce Unicode dashes in new copy.
- Leave ASCII `-` alone; do not change code operators or CSS that already use `-`.
